NAME
    cls — Clear the terminal screen.

SYNOPSIS
    cls

DESCRIPTION
    The 'cls' command clears everything currently displayed in the terminal.

    It is an alias for the 'clear' command, because apparently one command
    for clearing the screen wasn't enough.

USAGE
    > cls
        Clears the terminal screen.

FUN FACTS
    - cls does exactly the same thing as clear.
    - It exists mainly for Windows users who are used to the command.
    - No files are deleted.
    - Your terminal history is not affected.

SEE ALSO
    clear(1), help(1), man(1)

